[00:00.00]I built a kingdom out of paper
[00:04.00]Every streetlight knew my name
[00:08.00]Now the bells keep time without me
[00:12.00]And the choir sings it anyway
[00:16.00]Gold on the walls, dust on the crown
[00:20.00]I hear the march but not the crowd
[00:24.00]If this is glory, keep the ending
[00:28.00]Let the drums say it out loud
[00:32.00]I used to call the morning mine
[00:36.00]I used to walk like I belonged
[00:40.00]The gates are open, no one waiting
[00:44.00]Still I try to hit that song
[00:48.00]Hold the note, hold the line
[00:52.00]Sing it like the room is yours
[00:56.00]One more chorus in the paper kingdom
